<title>USA: Motorola gets contracts in Nigeria, Yemen.</title>
<headline>Motorola gets contracts in Nigeria, Yemen.</headline>
<dateline>ARLINGTON HEIGHTS, Ill. 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Motorola Inc said its International Cellular Infrastructure Group won a contract to build the initial phase of Intercellular Nigeria Ltd's national wireless telephone network.</p>
<p>It also won a contract to install a Wireless Local Loop network in Yemen. The value of the contracts was not reported.</p>
<p>In Nigeria, the wireless local loop system will provide first-time telephone service to thousands of residents, Motorola said. The system in Yemen will be developed in three phases, with the first scheduled to be up and running by the end of the 1997 first quarter.</p>
<p>		  ((-- Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787))</p>
